WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:04.790
10.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.790
9.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:06.290
8.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:06.790
7.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:12.460
(TOGETHER) 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.580
Ghostwriter, Beyond the Page.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:17.080
Great.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.040
You're here.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.120
Welcome back to Ghostwriter, Beyond the Page episode 2.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:25.030
Today we're going to become explorers and journey

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.700
through the lush world beneath the tropical canopy

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.760
of The Jungle Book.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.130
However, I think our journey is going

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.530
to be delayed a little bit because Donna

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.880
has misplaced her bullet journal somewhere in her bedroom.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.130
I hope she finds it soon because she

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.940
needs it to write her story.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.130
So let's check in and see how she's doing.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.210
I know I had it when I was writing last night.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.070
Aha!

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.740
I knew it was in here somewhere.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.760
There's so many important things in here.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.519
I don't know what I would do without it.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:06.270
Hey!

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.090
Speaking of important stuff, I finished my character

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.030
descriptions.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:11.550
OK.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:12.510
Check this out.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.540
A smart young girl with an amazing eye for color,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.430
patterns, all things fashion.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.110
They say write what you know, right?

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.690
She's talented at sewing and weaving,

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.750
but she has a hard time feeling like she fits in,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.570
especially when her sporty older brother treats her

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:29.820
like a little kid in front of all their friends.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.100
While I was brainstorming I thought

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.310
there should be a reason why Sapphire my character's name,

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.330
is so good at making threads.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.730
And then it hit me.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.890
Sapphire should be a spider.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.430
And her older brother Spelman is a star soccer player,

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.160
because with eight legs, he can really kick.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.290
The only thing is the world of a spider

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.160
is so different than mine.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:55.690
I mean, for them, everything is literally larger than life.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.080
I hope I can do her justice.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.700
Here, I even drew a picture of her.

00:02:10.419 --> 00:02:11.890
Where?

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.740
Well, that came out of nowhere.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.640
This has to be Ghostwriter with more help for my story.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.550
All right, let's see.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.680
Where?

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.860
Well, good thing I already found out where my journal was.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.497
Where?

00:02:39.497 --> 00:02:39.997
Where?

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.850
Oh, what in the world?

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.755
What are you looking for, my friend?

00:02:45.755 --> 00:02:48.440
Mowgli, what a nice surprise.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.790
Clearly, Ghostwriter knows I need help.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.400
Donna, it is good to see you.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.110
You, too, Mowgli.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.640
Where are you?

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.340
I'm exploring the jungle, searching for a new place

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.150
to call home.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.480
Oh, so you're not with your wolf family.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.260
No.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:06.230
It has become important for me to find

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:09.260
a place of my own, a new home.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.380
My wolf family will always love me and be there for me,

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.320
and I will always be a part of the pack.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.710
But I must now spread my wings and find a new place

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.680
where I belong, somewhere that protects my wolf family

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.410
and my human family from Shere Khan,

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:29.390
and somewhere I can truly become the human cub I'm meant to be.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:30.380
Wow.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.680
So it sounds like it's important to find a place that you

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.180
feel like you belong.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.500
Yes, exactly.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.430
I think you can't really know who you are if you

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.170
don't know where you belong.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.100
That makes sense.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.310
Well, I don't want to keep you from your search.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:49.760
Yes, I must continue before the sun dips below the trees.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.760
Take care, Donna.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:53.360
OK.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.550
I really think I get this one.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:57.650
What Mowgli said must be true.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:02.360
If where is so close to who, I need to figure out the where

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.770
for Sapphire.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:04.910
I have to create a setting.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.050
I forgot that Mowgli forges his own path

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:14.010
at the end of the book, but let's see what happens first.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:14.860
"Ow!"

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.600
Mowgli rolled over and was poked in the back by a branch.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.089
He opened his eyes and sighed.

00:04:21.089 --> 00:04:23.880
He'd hope to wake up safe and snuggled between his sleeping

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.600
brothers, warm in their fur.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.910
Instead, he was exactly where he was the night before.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.650
Out in the middle of the jungle.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.420
Chased off by his own pack.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.700
Twigs and branches from the tent he'd made

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.140
tumbled onto his head.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:40.560
Mowgli gave a sniff and rubbed his arm across his nose.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.160
[MONKEYS CHIRPING]

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.870
"Why the long face, friend?"

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.760
a voice chittered overhead.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.410
"Yeah, why so sad?"

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.120
called another voice.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.560
Mowgli looked up.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.820
"Who's there?"

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.560
"Oh, everyone."

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.850
"And no one."

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.200
"Just us, you see.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.432
The monkeys!"

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:03.500
[MONKEYS CHIRPING]

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:07.800
What in the world?

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:16.910
Sure enough, several little monkeys with wide grins

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.100
peered down at him from the trees.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:22.760
They dangled on matted, wildly spiked tails.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.040
Mowgli had seen them swinging through the treetops

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.200
and nibbling on sweet bananas.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.380
He'd wanted to play with them, but his mother disapproved.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:34.250
She called them "little troublemakers"

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.160
Mowgli felt a pang in his heart at the thought of his parents,

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:38.810
then shook it away.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.340
They weren't here now.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.990
They told him to leave.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:45.220
They didn't have the right to decide what he did anymore.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:48.100
As soon as he thought that, he felt ashamed.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:48.970
No.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.820
Being mad at his parents wasn't the answer.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.130
This was Shere Khan's fault.

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.110
"Cheer up!" one of the monkeys chirped,

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:59.350
handing him a ripe mango.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.750
Mowgli was surprised and a little pleased

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.660
to have someone looking out for him.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:04.160
"Yeah!

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.340
Cheer up!" called another monkey.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.900
"We think you're cool!"

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.760
"How did you make that log cave?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.190
Looks quite snuggly-- eek!"

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:14.770
The first monkey nearly toppled out of the tree

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.320
as a large, furry brown paw knocked the trunk.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.330
"Oops."

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.120
A shaggy sloth bear lumbered into view.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.920
"I must have slipped."

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:24.790
"Baloo!"

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.650
Mowgli exclaimed happily.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.630
"Why are you here, too?"

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:32.530
Along with Bagheera, Baloo was Mowgli's other best friend.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.840
Baloo scratched his round belly.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.880
"Bagheera was worried about you wandering off,"

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.490
he explained, patting Mowgli's head.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:41.860
"I showed up while you were sleeping last night.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.650
He left me to watch you until he gets back."

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.930
"Bagheera shouldn't worry," Mowgli said,

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.840
but he was secretly glad his friends were with him.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.040
"I'm fine.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.230
Don't you have better things to do?"

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:55.030
"Good friends never leave you alone,"

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:57.160
Bagheera called from behind them.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.370
The panther sauntered up and carefully dropped a banana

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.140
from between his teeth.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:03.070
"Eat that.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:04.690
You're a growing cub.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.750
Now, why are you talking to the monkeys?"

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:10.120
"They seem nice," Mowgli said, breaking up

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.760
a chunk of the banana and walking with his friends.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.530
"They gave me this mango."

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.910
Baloo sniffed.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.470
"They seem nice for now.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.000
Just you wait.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.140
Listen, Mowgli.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:23.980
We've taught you a lot of the ways of the jungle, right?"

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:24.940
"Right!"

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.940
"And we've never steered you wrong, right?"

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:28.750
"Of course!"

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.400
Mowgli said firmly.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.650
"You've been my teachers for years.

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:35.440
You guys know everything about the jungle."

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:36.250
"That's right."

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.330
Bagheera purred proudly.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.480
I never realized how much The Jungle Book

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.850
focuses on finding home.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:48.720
From the wolf pack to the monkey kingdom to the village,

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.693
there are a lot of important places along Mowgli's journey.

00:07:52.693 --> 00:07:54.360
I've got some thinking to do about where

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.280
my character will live.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.950
Maybe she'll be trying to find it, just like Mowgli.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.380
Well, let's dive right in.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:10.480
If you want to dive deeper into the Ghostwriter world,

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:13.450
be sure to read The Jungle Book.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.550
And then when you're finished, the Jungle

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:18.100
Ghost section of the activity guide.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.010
And of course, be sure to check in with the Ghostwriter gang

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.960
on Apple TV+ for episodes of the show.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.350
So thank you for exploring with me today.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:27.997
And I can't wait for you to come back

00:08:27.997 --> 00:08:29.830
next time when we're going to see what Donna

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:32.110
and Ghostwriter are up to next.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.750
Bye bye.

